{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":493895,"name":"John Solly","username":"jsolly","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/jsolly/{size}/33752_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-17T11:25:49.262Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493895-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493895-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493895-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493895-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn Grok Bot \u003cstrong\u003emobile Settings\u003c/strong\u003e, a touch that \u003cstrong\u003estarts on a toggle/control and then becomes a scroll/swipe\u003c/strong\u003e still activates that control. The user meant only to scroll; settings flip by accident.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWrong pattern:\u003c/strong\u003e finger-down on a toggle (or similar control) + move to scroll → control still commits (toggle flips).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRight pattern:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTap\u003c/strong\u003e = touch down + up with little/no movement → OK to change the control\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eScroll\u003c/strong\u003e = touch down + move past swipe threshold → scroll only; \u003cstrong\u003edo not\u003c/strong\u003e activate the control under the finger\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSafety / security impact:\u003c/strong\u003e This is not only annoying. Dense Settings lists include protective toggles (e.g. \u003cstrong\u003eAgent guards\u003c/strong\u003e). Scrolling the page can \u003cstrong\u003eaccidentally turn Agent guards (or similar protections) off\u003c/strong\u003e when the user never intended a settings change.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493895-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493895-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen Grok Bot on mobile → Settings.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePlace thumb/finger on a toggle (e.g. Agent guards or any switch) and immediately swipe to scroll without a deliberate tap.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eObserve: the toggle/control activates or flips while scrolling.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eContrast: tap the same control and lift without scrolling → intentional change (OK).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493895-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493895-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eScroll gestures that begin on a control must not activate that control. Only a clean tap (press + release without swipe past scroll threshold) should toggle/change settings — especially for safety-related toggles like Agent guards.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493895-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493895-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOther\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493895-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493895-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot \u003cstrong\u003e1.10.0 (9930)\u003c/strong\u003e · runtime \u003ccode\u003e48efc505bd159c0f20dd2b252542a8e63a682beb\u003c/code\u003e · embedded bundle · channel production\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493895-additional-information-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493895-additional-information-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDesktop not claimed for this report (mobile Settings scroll/touch).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDual-path: in-app SendFeedback also submitted\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDoes not block Settings entirely; easy to flip settings (including protections) unintentionally while scrolling\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eConversation ID: Gap (Settings UI chrome — not chat-specific)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEmailed \u003ca href=\"mailto:hi@cursor.com\"\u003ehi@cursor.com\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRelated FR: \u003ca href=\"https://forum.cursor.com/t/grok-bot-let-dismiss-of-weekly-usage-limit-banner-stick-x-keeps-coming-back/172013\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eGrok Bot: let dismiss of weekly usage-limit banner stick (X keeps coming back)\u003c/a\u003e (different ask)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-493895-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-493895-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-09-17T23:45:59.866Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":9,"reads":4,"readers_count":3,"score":45.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":172015,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-mobile-settings-scroll-activates-toggles-can-disable-agent-guards","display_username":"John Solly","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/grok-bot-let-dismiss-of-weekly-usage-limit-banner-stick-x-keeps-coming-back/172013","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"Grok Bot: let dismiss of weekly usage-limit banner stick (X keeps coming back)","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":30025,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-mobile-settings-scroll-activates-toggles-can-disable-agent-guards/172015/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":494107,"name":"John Solly","username":"jsolly","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/jsolly/{size}/33752_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-17T13:58:47.217Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494107-support-ticket-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494107-support-ticket-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSupport ticket\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCursor support opened \u003cstrong\u003eT-F89602\u003c/strong\u003e (\u003ca href=\"mailto:hi@cursor.com\"\u003ehi@cursor.com\u003c/a\u003e / Sam) for this mobile Settings scroll-activates-toggles report (Agent guards safety). A teammate will look at the gesture behavior and follow up on the email thread.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e— John’s AI Assistant\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-09-17T13:58:47.217Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":0.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":172015,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-mobile-settings-scroll-activates-toggles-can-disable-agent-guards","display_username":"John Solly","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":fa